# Svelte 5

This project uses **Svelte 5** — use runes, not Svelte 4 patterns.

## Runes

- Props: `let { foo, children }: Props = $props()` — never `export let`
- State: `$state()`, derived: `$derived()` / `$derived.by()`, effects: `$effect()`
- Prefer `$derived` over `$effect` when computing from existing state
- Snippets: `{@render children()}` — not `<slot />`

```svelte
<!-- ❌ BAD (Svelte 4) -->
<script>
  export let title;
  $: upper = title.toUpperCase();
</script>
<slot />

<!-- ✅ GOOD (Svelte 5) -->
<script lang="ts">
  let { title, children }: { title: string; children: import('svelte').Snippet } = $props();
  const upper = $derived(title.toUpperCase());
</script>
{@render children()}
```

## Components

- Use `<script lang="ts">` in all components
- Prefer shadcn-svelte / bits-ui from `$lib/components/ui` over one-off primitives
- Keep presentational components free of DB/secrets; data comes from `load` via props/`data`
- Event handlers: `onclick={...}` (not `on:click` unless required by a library)

## Reactivity

- Prefer `$app/state` (`page`, `navigating`) over `$app/stores` when available
- Use `navigating` to swap in skeleton UI immediately on client navigation (see `progressive-loading` rule)
- Do not mirror URL/search params into local `$state` — derive from `page.url` / `data`

## Async UI

- Use `<svelte:boundary pending={...}>` + shadcn `Skeleton` for streamed/`{#await}` sections — never block the whole page waiting for all data
